@startuml state_reservation
title Increment 5 - Reservation State Diagram (Approved Policies)

hide empty description

[*] --> Pending : Valid request / atomic 5-minute hold created

Pending --> Pending : Payment fails / retry until original deadline
Pending --> Confirmed : Simulated payment succeeds\n[before expiresAt and DB commit succeeds]
Pending --> Expired : now >= expiresAt / release held inventory
Pending --> Cancelled : Guest explicitly cancels payment / release hold

Confirmed --> CheckedIn : Receptionist verifies identity\nand assigns suitable physical room
CheckedIn --> CheckedOut : Receptionist completes check-out
Confirmed --> Cancelled : Eligible cancellation before check-in\n/ release inventory; apply refund policy
Confirmed --> NoShow : No arrival by 12:00 noon\non day after scheduled check-in

Expired --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]
NoShow --> [*]
CheckedOut --> [*]

note right of Pending
  This is a persisted temporary reservation.
  Holds room-type inventory, NOT a room number.
  expiresAt = server creation time + 5 minutes.
  Payment retries never extend the deadline.
  A failed payment does not change the state.
end note

note right of Confirmed
  Requires successful simulated payment,
  valid unexpired hold, and database commit.
  Booking reference and random secret code
  are issued; only the code hash is stored.
end note

note bottom of Cancelled
  Confirmed booking: cancellation permitted
  before scheduled check-in (14:00 local time).
  >= 24 hours before: 100% simulated refund.
  < 24 hours before: no refund.
  Pending cancellation simply releases the hold.
end note

note right of NoShow
  No show if not checked in by 12:00 noon
  the following day; no simulated refund.
  Release capacity for remaining future nights.
end note

@enduml
